---
import DocsLayout from "@/layouts/DocsLayout.astro"

const html =
  '<p>KoAkademy provides an authenticated <strong>Model Context Protocol (MCP)</strong> HTTP server that enables AI agents (such as OpenCode, Claude Desktop, Cursor, or custom assistants) to query and modify school administration data safely.</p>\n<p>Every tool invocation runs under the authenticated user&#39;s account, enforces tenant school scoping, and honors fine-grained application permissions.</p>\n<h2>Endpoint &amp; Transport</h2>\n<p>KoAkademy implements the MCP specification (<code>2025-11-25</code>) over HTTP transport using JSON-RPC 2.0.</p>\n<pre><code class="language-text">POST /mcp/koakademy\n</code></pre>\n<h3>Request Headers</h3>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Header</th>\n<th>Description</th>\n<th>Required</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>Authorization</code></td>\n<td><code>Bearer &lt;sanctum_personal_access_token&gt;</code></td>\n<td><strong>Yes</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Content-Type</code></td>\n<td><code>application/json</code></td>\n<td><strong>Yes</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Accept</code></td>\n<td><code>application/json</code></td>\n<td><strong>Yes</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>X-KoAkademy-School</code></td>\n<td>ID of the school to scope operations to</td>\n<td>Optional (defaults to caller&#39;s primary school)</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<h3>Rate Limiting</h3>\n<p>The MCP endpoint is rate-limited by default to <strong>30 requests per minute</strong> per user or IP address (<code>throttle:mcp</code>). This can be customized via the <code>MCP_RATE_LIMIT</code> environment variable in <code>config/api.php</code>.</p>\n<hr>\n<h2>Authentication &amp; Token Abilities</h2>\n<p>MCP requests require personal access tokens issued via Laravel Sanctum from the user&#39;s <strong>Profile / Accounts &amp; Security</strong> settings under <strong>Developer API &amp; MCP Keys</strong>.</p>\n<h3>Dedicated MCP Abilities</h3>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Token Ability</th>\n<th>Scope</th>\n<th>Capabilities</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>mcp:read</code></td>\n<td>Read-only</td>\n<td>Allows AI agents to execute read-only queries (<code>get_my_context</code>, <code>get_student_profile</code>, <code>search_students</code>, <code>get_student_schedule</code>, <code>get_enrollment_status</code>, <code>list_student_enrollments</code>, <code>get_student_subject_enrollments</code>, <code>get_course_curriculum</code>, <code>get_available_subjects</code>, etc.). Students can query their own data; staff can query school records.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>mcp:write</code></td>\n<td>Mutating</td>\n<td>Allows AI agents to execute write operations (<code>verify_enrollment_requirement</code>, <code>advance_enrollment_step</code>, <code>update_enrollment_remarks</code>, <code>enroll_student_subject</code>, <code>update_subject_enrollment_grade</code>, <code>drop_student_subject_enrollment</code>). Restricted to staff/admin accounts and requires <code>mcp:read</code>.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>A token with <code>mcp:write</code> alone without <code>mcp:read</code> is automatically rejected. Wildcard <code>*</code> tokens are strictly prohibited for MCP endpoints.</p>\n<h3>Administrative &amp; Role Gating</h3>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>User Role Gating:</strong> Staff, faculty, and administrative accounts with Developer Mode enabled can issue both <code>mcp:read</code> and <code>mcp:write</code> keys. Students in Developer Mode can issue <code>mcp:read</code> tokens to query their personal academic records; student accounts are prevented from issuing <code>mcp:write</code> keys.</li>\n<li><strong>Global MCP Switch:</strong> Administrators can disable the MCP server entirely via <strong>Settings -&gt; API &amp; Integrations -&gt; Model Context Protocol (MCP)</strong> or via <code>MCP_ENABLED=false</code> in <code>.env</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>Global Mutation Switch:</strong> Administrators can allow or disallow mutating tools globally (<code>mcp_write_enabled</code>). When disabled, write tools return an actionable error without executing changes, and <code>get_my_context</code> reports <code>mcp.can_write: false</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>Tool-Level RBAC:</strong> Even with an <code>mcp:write</code> token, an agent cannot perform actions that the issuing staff account does not have permission to execute (e.g., verifying requirements or enrolling subjects requires <code>Update:StudentEnrollment</code>; viewing billing requires <code>View:Cashier</code> or <code>view_tuition_fees</code>).</li>\n</ol>\n<hr>\n<h2>Tool Catalog</h2>\n<p>KoAkademy registers 22 core tools across five domain categories.</p>\n<h3>1. Context &amp; School Overview</h3>\n<h4><code>get_my_context</code></h4>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Access:</strong> Read-only (<code>mcp:read</code>)</li>\n<li><strong>Description:</strong> Returns the authenticated caller&#39;s identity, active school, current academic period, and available curriculum capabilities. Agents should invoke this tool first.</li>\n<li><strong>Arguments:</strong> None</li>\n<li><strong>Sample Response:</strong><pre><code class="language-json">{\n  &quot;user&quot;: { &quot;id&quot;: 14, &quot;name&quot;: &quot;Maria Santos&quot;, &quot;role&quot;: &quot;registrar&quot; },\n  &quot;school&quot;: { &quot;id&quot;: 1, &quot;name&quot;: &quot;School of Computer Studies&quot;, &quot;code&quot;: &quot;SCS&quot; },\n  &quot;academic_period&quot;: { &quot;school_year&quot;: &quot;2026 - 2027&quot;, &quot;semester&quot;: 1 },\n  &quot;mcp&quot;: { &quot;token_name&quot;: &quot;OpenCode Assistant&quot;, &quot;can_write&quot;: true }\n}\n</code></pre>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h4><code>get_school_details</code></h4>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Access:</strong> Read-only (<code>mcp:read</code>)</li>\n<li><strong>Description:</strong> Retrieves organization metadata for the active school, including contact info, dean details, curriculum frameworks, and active departments.</li>\n<li><strong>Arguments:</strong> None</li>\n</ul>\n<h4><code>get_school_metrics</code></h4>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Access:</strong> Read-only (<code>mcp:read</code>) · <strong>Restricted to Administrators</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Description:</strong> Returns operational KPI statistics for the current academic period (total students, enrolled count, applicants, graduated students, active classes, and total faculty).</li>\n<li><strong>Arguments:</strong> None</li>\n<li><strong>Sample Response:</strong><pre><code class="language-json">{\n  &quot;metrics&quot;: {\n    &quot;total_students&quot;: 1420,\n    &quot;enrolled_students&quot;: 1180,\n    &quot;applicants&quot;: 185,\n    &quot;graduated_students&quot;: 55,\n    &quot;enrolled_this_period&quot;: 1120,\n    &quot;pending_enrollments&quot;: 48,\n    &quot;active_classes&quot;: 164,\n    &quot;total_faculty&quot;: 62\n  }\n}\n</code></pre>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<hr>\n<h3>2. Student &amp; Faculty Directory</h3>\n<h4><code>get_student_profile</code></h4>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Access:</strong> Read-only (<code>mcp:read</code>) · <strong>Requires <code>View:Student</code> for staff; students can query their own record</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Description:</strong> Retrieves the detailed academic profile of a student, including student number, LRN, degree program, academic year level, contact details, clearance status, and enrollment status.</li>\n<li><strong>Arguments:</strong><ul>\n<li><code>student_id</code> (integer, optional): The database ID or school student number. Optional for student callers (defaults to their own profile).</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Sample Response:</strong><pre><code class="language-json">{\n  &quot;id&quot;: 42,\n  &quot;student_number&quot;: &quot;202611&quot;,\n  &quot;name&quot;: &quot;Eduardo Reyes&quot;,\n  &quot;email&quot;: &quot;eduardo.reyes@student.koakademy.edu&quot;,\n  &quot;status&quot;: &quot;enrolled&quot;,\n  &quot;clearance_status&quot;: &quot;cleared&quot;,\n  &quot;academic_year&quot;: 2,\n  &quot;course&quot;: { &quot;id&quot;: 3, &quot;code&quot;: &quot;BSCS&quot;, &quot;title&quot;: &quot;Computer Science&quot; }\n}\n</code></pre>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h4><code>search_students</code></h4>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Access:</strong> Read-only (<code>mcp:read</code>) · <strong>Requires <code>ViewAny:Student</code></strong></li>\n<li><strong>Description:</strong> Searches students in the active school by name, student number, or email. Results are bounded and omit sensitive personal data.</li>\n<li><strong>Arguments:</strong><ul>\n<li><code>query</code> (string, required, 2-100 chars): Search term.</li>\n<li><code>limit</code> (integer, optional, 1-25, default: 10): Maximum results.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h4><code>get_student_schedule</code></h4>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Access:</strong> Read-only (<code>mcp:read</code>) · <strong>Requires <code>View:Student</code> for staff; students can query their own schedule</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Description:</strong> Retrieves a student&#39;s active class enrollments, meeting days, room assignments, instructor names, and any detected schedule time overlaps.</li>\n<li><strong>Arguments:</strong><ul>\n<li><code>student_id</code> (integer, required): Internal ID returned by <code>search_students</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h4><code>search_faculty</code></h4>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Access:</strong> Read-only (<code>mcp:read</code>) · <strong>Requires <code>ViewAny:Faculty</code></strong></li>\n<li><strong>Description:</strong> Searches faculty members in the active school by name, department, or faculty ID number.</li>\n<li><strong>Arguments:</strong><ul>\n<li><code>query</code> (string, required, 2-100 chars): Search term.</li>\n<li><code>limit</code> (integer, optional, 1-25, default: 10): Maximum results.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<hr>\n<h3>3. Academic Curriculum &amp; Subjects</h3>\n<h4><code>get_course_curriculum</code></h4>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Access:</strong> Read-only (<code>mcp:read</code>) · <strong>Requires <code>View:Course</code> for staff; open to enrolled students</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Description:</strong> Returns the complete curriculum of an academic program or course broken down by year level and semester with lecture/lab units, prerequisite codes, and credit types.</li>\n<li><strong>Arguments:</strong><ul>\n<li><code>course_id</code> (integer, required): Course / program ID.</li>\n<li><code>year_level</code> (integer, optional, 1-6): Filter by academic year.</li>\n<li><code>semester</code> (integer, optional, 1 or 2): Filter by semester.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h4><code>get_available_subjects</code></h4>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Access:</strong> Read-only (<code>mcp:read</code>) · <strong>Requires <code>View:Student</code> for staff; students can query their own eligibility</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Description:</strong> Inspects curriculum requirements for a student&#39;s program and determines which subjects they are eligible to take, distinguishing between completed, currently enrolled, and available subjects.</li>\n<li><strong>Arguments:</strong><ul>\n<li><code>student_id</code> (integer, optional): Student ID. Defaults to caller if student.</li>\n<li><code>year_level</code> (integer, optional): Year level to evaluate. Defaults to student&#39;s current year.</li>\n<li><code>semester</code> (integer, optional, 1 or 2): Defaults to current semester.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h4><code>list_academic_offerings</code></h4>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Access:</strong> Read-only (<code>mcp:read</code>) · <strong>Requires <code>ViewAny:Course</code> and <code>ViewAny:Classes</code></strong></li>\n<li><strong>Description:</strong> Lists active academic programs and scheduled classes with section codes, faculty assignments, rooms, and enrolled capacity for the specified academic period.</li>\n<li><strong>Arguments:</strong><ul>\n<li><code>school_year</code> (string, optional): e.g. <code>&quot;2026 - 2027&quot;</code>. Defaults to current period.</li>\n<li><code>semester</code> (integer, optional, <code>1</code> or <code>2</code>): Defaults to current period.</li>\n<li><code>limit</code> (integer, optional, 1-50, default: 25): Result cap per collection.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<hr>\n<h3>4. Enrollments &amp; Subject Enrollments</h3>\n<h4><code>list_student_enrollments</code></h4>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Access:</strong> Read-only (<code>mcp:read</code>) · <strong>Requires <code>View:StudentEnrollment</code> for staff; students can query their own records</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Description:</strong> Lists all semester enrollment records for a student across their academic history with term, status, runtime, downpayment, and submission channel.</li>\n<li><strong>Arguments:</strong><ul>\n<li><code>student_id</code> (integer, optional): Student database ID or student number. Defaults to caller if student.</li>\n<li><code>limit</code> (integer, optional, 1-50, default: 20): Maximum records.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h4><code>get_enrollment_status</code></h4>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Access:</strong> Read-only (<code>mcp:read</code>) · <strong>Requires <code>View:StudentEnrollment</code></strong></li>\n<li><strong>Description:</strong> Retrieves detailed workflow state, academic period, program, and all checklist requirements (pending, verified, or waived) for an enrollment record.</li>\n<li><strong>Arguments:</strong><ul>\n<li><code>enrollment_id</code> (integer, required): Enrollment record ID.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h4><code>get_student_subject_enrollments</code></h4>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Access:</strong> Read-only (<code>mcp:read</code>) · <strong>Requires <code>View:StudentEnrollment</code> for staff; students can query their own subjects</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Description:</strong> Retrieves the subjects a student is enrolled in for a specific enrollment record or academic term, returning subject code, title, units, class section, instructor, grades, and remarks.</li>\n<li><strong>Arguments:</strong><ul>\n<li><code>enrollment_id</code> (integer, optional): Target enrollment record ID.</li>\n<li><code>student_id</code> (integer, optional): Target student ID.</li>\n<li><code>school_year</code> (string, optional): e.g. <code>&quot;2026 - 2027&quot;</code>. Defaults to current term.</li>\n<li><code>semester</code> (integer, optional, 1 or 2): Defaults to current semester.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h4><code>enroll_student_subject</code></h4>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Access:</strong> Mutation (<code>mcp:write</code>) · <strong>Requires <code>Update:StudentEnrollment</code></strong></li>\n<li><strong>Description:</strong> Enrolls a student in an academic subject under an enrollment record, optionally assigning a scheduled class section. Automatically synchronizes class enrollments.</li>\n<li><strong>Arguments:</strong><ul>\n<li><code>enrollment_id</code> (integer, required): ID of the student enrollment.</li>\n<li><code>subject_id</code> (integer, required): ID of the curriculum subject to add.</li>\n<li><code>class_id</code> (integer, optional): Scheduled class ID to assign a specific schedule and section.</li>\n<li><code>section</code> (string, optional): Section name override if class_id is omitted.</li>\n<li><code>is_modular</code> (boolean, optional): Modular learning flag.</li>\n<li><code>idempotency_key</code> (string, required, 1-96 chars): Unique key to guarantee safe replay.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h4><code>update_subject_enrollment_grade</code></h4>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Access:</strong> Mutation (<code>mcp:write</code>) · <strong>Requires <code>Update:StudentEnrollment</code></strong></li>\n<li><strong>Description:</strong> Records or updates official grades (prelim, midterm, finals, or overall grade) and evaluation remarks on an enrolled subject.</li>\n<li><strong>Arguments:</strong><ul>\n<li><code>subject_enrollment_id</code> (integer, required): ID of the <code>subject_enrollment</code> record.</li>\n<li><code>grade</code> (number, optional): Final/overall grade score.</li>\n<li><code>prelim_grade</code> (number, optional): Prelim exam/term grade score.</li>\n<li><code>midterm_grade</code> (number, optional): Midterm exam/term grade score.</li>\n<li><code>finals_grade</code> (number, optional): Final exam/term grade score.</li>\n<li><code>remarks</code> (string, optional): e.g. <code>&quot;Passed&quot;</code>, <code>&quot;Failed&quot;</code>, <code>&quot;Incomplete&quot;</code>.</li>\n<li><code>idempotency_key</code> (string, required, 1-96 chars): Unique key to guarantee safe replay.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h4><code>drop_student_subject_enrollment</code></h4>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Access:</strong> Mutation (<code>mcp:write</code>) · <strong>Requires <code>Update:StudentEnrollment</code></strong></li>\n<li><strong>Description:</strong> Drops or removes an enrolled subject from a student&#39;s enrollment record and automatically releases any linked class seat.</li>\n<li><strong>Arguments:</strong><ul>\n<li><code>subject_enrollment_id</code> (integer, required): ID of the <code>subject_enrollment</code> record to drop.</li>\n<li><code>reason</code> (string, required, max 1000 chars): Documented reason for dropping the subject.</li>\n<li><code>idempotency_key</code> (string, required, 1-96 chars): Unique key to guarantee safe replay.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h4><code>list_pending_enrollments</code></h4>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Access:</strong> Read-only (<code>mcp:read</code>) · <strong>Restricted to Administrators · Requires <code>ViewAny:StudentEnrollment</code></strong></li>\n<li><strong>Description:</strong> Lists enrollments currently awaiting administrative review, departmental verification, or cashier approval.</li>\n<li><strong>Arguments:</strong><ul>\n<li><code>status</code> (string, optional): Filter by status (e.g. <code>&quot;submitted&quot;</code>, <code>&quot;department_verification&quot;</code>). Omit to list all incomplete enrollments.</li>\n<li><code>course_id</code> (integer, optional): Filter by program.</li>\n<li><code>limit</code> (integer, optional, 1-50, default: 20): Result cap.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h4><code>get_enrollment_audit_trail</code></h4>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Access:</strong> Read-only (<code>mcp:read</code>) · <strong>Requires <code>View:StudentEnrollment</code></strong></li>\n<li><strong>Description:</strong> Returns the complete historical timeline of workflow events, state transitions, requirement verifications, and waivers with actor details and audit reasons.</li>\n<li><strong>Arguments:</strong><ul>\n<li><code>enrollment_id</code> (integer, required): Enrollment record ID.</li>\n<li><code>limit</code> (integer, optional, 1-50, default: 25): Event count.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h4><code>advance_enrollment_step</code></h4>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Access:</strong> Mutation (<code>mcp:write</code>) · <strong>Restricted to Administrators · Requires <code>Update:StudentEnrollment</code></strong></li>\n<li><strong>Description:</strong> Advances an enrollment to its next workflow step or executes an explicit policy transition with guaranteed idempotency.</li>\n<li><strong>Arguments:</strong><ul>\n<li><code>enrollment_id</code> (integer, required): Enrollment record ID.</li>\n<li><code>transition_key</code> (string, optional): Target transition identifier for policy-based workflows.</li>\n<li><code>reason</code> (string, optional, max 1000 chars): Audit reason for the transition.</li>\n<li><code>idempotency_key</code> (string, required, 1-96 chars): Client-supplied unique token to guarantee safe retries.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h4><code>verify_enrollment_requirement</code></h4>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Access:</strong> Mutation (<code>mcp:write</code>) · <strong>Requires <code>Update:StudentEnrollment</code></strong></li>\n<li><strong>Description:</strong> Marks a pending document or enrollment requirement as verified. Waived requirements cannot be verified.</li>\n<li><strong>Arguments:</strong><ul>\n<li><code>requirement_id</code> (integer, required): Enrollment requirement ID from <code>get_enrollment_status</code>.</li>\n<li><code>idempotency_key</code> (string, required, 1-96 chars): Client-supplied unique token to guarantee safe retries.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h4><code>update_enrollment_remarks</code></h4>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Access:</strong> Mutation (<code>mcp:write</code>) · <strong>Requires <code>Update:StudentEnrollment</code></strong></li>\n<li><strong>Description:</strong> Updates administrative notes or registrar remarks on an enrollment record.</li>\n<li><strong>Arguments:</strong><ul>\n<li><code>enrollment_id</code> (integer, required): Enrollment record ID.</li>\n<li><code>remarks</code> (string, required, max 2000 chars): Updated remarks text.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<hr>\n<h3>5. Billing &amp; Finance</h3>\n<h4><code>get_statement_of_account</code></h4>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Access:</strong> Read-only (<code>mcp:read</code>) · <strong>Requires <code>View:Cashier</code> or <code>view_tuition_fees</code></strong></li>\n<li><strong>Description:</strong> Calculates the verified statement of account for an enrollment, including base tuition, laboratory fees, miscellaneous fees, applied discounts, verified payments, and remaining balance due.</li>\n<li><strong>Arguments:</strong><ul>\n<li><code>enrollment_id</code> (integer, required): Enrollment record ID.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<hr>\n<h2>Client Configuration Guides</h2>\n<h3>1. OpenCode</h3>\n<p>Add the server to your OpenCode configuration (e.g. <code>opencode.json</code> or <code>.opencode/settings.json</code>):</p>\n<pre><code class="language-json">{\n  &quot;mcp&quot;: {\n    &quot;servers&quot;: {\n      &quot;koakademy&quot;: {\n        &quot;url&quot;: &quot;https://your-school.edu/mcp/koakademy&quot;,\n        &quot;headers&quot;: {\n          &quot;Authorization&quot;: &quot;Bearer 3|xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx&quot;,\n          &quot;X-KoAkademy-School&quot;: &quot;1&quot;\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n</code></pre>\n<h3>2. Claude Desktop</h3>\n<p>In <code>claude_desktop_config.json</code>:</p>\n<pre><code class="language-json">{\n  &quot;mcpServers&quot;: {\n    &quot;koakademy&quot;: {\n      &quot;url&quot;: &quot;https://your-school.edu/mcp/koakademy&quot;,\n      &quot;headers&quot;: {\n        &quot;Authorization&quot;: &quot;Bearer YOUR_SANCTUM_TOKEN&quot;,\n        &quot;X-KoAkademy-School&quot;: &quot;1&quot;\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n</code></pre>\n<h3>3. Cursor</h3>\n<p>In <code>.cursor/mcp.json</code>:</p>\n<pre><code class="language-json">{\n  &quot;mcpServers&quot;: {\n    &quot;koakademy&quot;: {\n      &quot;url&quot;: &quot;https://your-school.edu/mcp/koakademy&quot;,\n      &quot;headers&quot;: {\n        &quot;Authorization&quot;: &quot;Bearer YOUR_SANCTUM_TOKEN&quot;\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n</code></pre>\n<h3>4. Direct HTTP / cURL Example</h3>\n<p>To list available tools:</p>\n<pre><code class="language-bash">curl -X POST https://your-school.edu/mcp/koakademy \\\n  -H &quot;Authorization: Bearer YOUR_SANCTUM_TOKEN&quot; \\\n  -H &quot;Content-Type: application/json&quot; \\\n  -H &quot;Accept: application/json&quot; \\\n  -H &quot;X-KoAkademy-School: 1&quot; \\\n  -d &#39;{\n    &quot;jsonrpc&quot;: &quot;2.0&quot;,\n    &quot;id&quot;: 1,\n    &quot;method&quot;: &quot;tools/list&quot;,\n    &quot;params&quot;: {}\n  }&#39;\n</code></pre>\n<p>To call a tool:</p>\n<pre><code class="language-bash">curl -X POST https://your-school.edu/mcp/koakademy \\\n  -H &quot;Authorization: Bearer YOUR_SANCTUM_TOKEN&quot; \\\n  -H &quot;Content-Type: application/json&quot; \\\n  -H &quot;Accept: application/json&quot; \\\n  -d &#39;{\n    &quot;jsonrpc&quot;: &quot;2.0&quot;,\n    &quot;id&quot;: 2,\n    &quot;method&quot;: &quot;tools/call&quot;,\n    &quot;params&quot;: {\n      &quot;name&quot;: &quot;search_students&quot;,\n      &quot;arguments&quot;: {\n        &quot;query&quot;: &quot;Maria&quot;\n      }\n    }\n  }&#39;\n</code></pre>\n'
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Model Context Protocol (MCP) Server"
  path="/api/mcp"
  description="Expose authorized KoAkademy student, academic, enrollment, and administrative tools to internal AI agents using the standard Model Context Protocol."
>
  <Fragment set:html={html} />
</DocsLayout>
